Third-party software linked into builds of this engine:

  Filament, by Google — Apache License 2.0.
  https://github.com/google/filament

  The renderer links Filament's libraries, so an application built with
  Orblit contains Filament code and carries its licence. This notice is that
  licence's requirement, not an attribution of design.

  A prebuilt Filament.xcframework is committed under
  packages/orblit_filament/darwin/orblit_filament/third_party/ because the
  current Xcode cannot regenerate it. That is redistribution rather than
  linking, so a full copy of the Apache License 2.0 is included at
  LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt, which is what section 4 of that licence asks for.

  ufbx, by Samuli Raivio — MIT License, or public domain (the Unlicense), at
  the user's choice.
  https://github.com/ufbx/ufbx

  The renderer compiles ufbx to read FBX and OBJ files, so an application
  built with Orblit contains ufbx code. Its source is vendored, unmodified,
  under packages/orblit_filament/darwin/orblit_filament/Sources/
  orblit_filament_native/third_party/ufbx/, which is redistribution; the MIT
  licence asks for its notice to travel with copies, and the licence file as
  ufbx ships it is at LICENSES/ufbx.txt.

  tinyexr, by Syoyo Fujita and contributors — BSD 3-Clause License, and the
  OpenEXR notice (Industrial Light & Magic, BSD-style) for the OpenEXR code
  it contains.
  https://github.com/syoyo/tinyexr

  miniz, by Rich Geldreich, RAD Game Tools and Valve Software — MIT License.
  https://github.com/richgel999/miniz

  The renderer compiles tinyexr, with miniz as its deflate, to read OpenEXR
  environments at run time. Both are vendored under
  packages/orblit_filament/darwin/orblit_filament/Sources/
  orblit_filament_native/third_party/ (tinyexr unmodified; miniz with one
  declaration moved so it compiles as C++), which is redistribution; their
  notices are at LICENSES/tinyexr.txt and LICENSES/miniz.txt.

Third-party software in the offline texture cooker only:

  packages/orblit_filament/native/texture_cook builds orblit_texture_cook, a
  build-machine tool. None of the following is linked into the renderer or
  into an application built with Orblit, and none of their source is
  committed here: native/texture_cook/fetch.sh fetches it, pinned by commit
  and checked against sources.sha256, when the tool is built. The notices
  are copied under LICENSES/ for anyone who distributes the tool itself.
  The textures it writes contain no code from any of them.

  Basis Universal 2.1.0r, by Binomial LLC — Apache License 2.0.
  https://github.com/BinomialLLC/basis_universal
  The licence is at LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt and its NOTICE, which section
  4(d) asks a redistribution to carry, at LICENSES/basis_universal-NOTICE.txt.

  Zstandard, by Facebook, Inc. (the copy Basis Universal carries) — BSD
  licence, at LICENSES/zstd.txt.
  https://github.com/facebook/zstd

  stb_image and stb_image_write, by Sean Barrett — MIT License, or public
  domain (the Unlicense), at the user's choice; at LICENSES/stb.txt.
  https://github.com/nothings/stb
